    "title": "Middle school restructuring approved in Pittsfield - NewsBreak",
    "text": "PITTSFIELD, Mass. ( NEWS10 ) — School leaders in Pittsfield voted on a proposal Wednesday that would impact the way middle school grade levels are structured. The vote passed, so now fifth and sixth graders will be grouped separately from seventh and eighth graders. Officials said the goal is to better support students transitioning out of elementary or into high school. The proposal would also impact current attendance zones. In addition to the vote, it was also the final board meeting for the superintendent, who has been in the role since 2021. Read the latest from NEWS10: NEWS10 is the Capital Region’s local news leader! For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to NEWS10 ABC.",
